# The repo root ignores `dist/` at every depth. This plugin is the exception, and the
# carve-out is load-bearing: Claude Code installs it by copying this directory out of a
# git clone. There is no `npm pack`, no build step, and no install hook, so an uncommitted
# `dist/` means the hooks are simply absent on every user's machine — and no test in this
# repo can see that, because the build works locally.
!dist/
